1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
This is the Statistics screen in TestingView —
where replay turns into hard numbers.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
At the top you get instant KPIs:
win rate, profit factor, average R:R…

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Sharpe ratio, expectancy,
max drawdown, and max run-up.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,500
In this run we’re looking at 57% win rate
and a 1.33 profit factor.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,500
But the real power is this:
every chart is clickable.

6
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:29,500
Click any tile to enlarge it
and drill into the details.

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:34,500
Open the equity curve
and highlight the win streak instantly.

8
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:39,500
Click Max Drawdown to see the exact dip —
5.6% and -$8,098 in this example.

9
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:46,000
And Max Time in Drawdown shows how long
you were underwater before recovery.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,500
Inside the enlarged performance view,
you’ve got a Forecast button.

11
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:56,500
One click shows an expectation range —
a fast sanity check for what’s “normal”.

12
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:02,500
Back on the dashboard:
Performance by Hour shows when you’re sharp…

13
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,500
…and when you’re leaking money.

14
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:10,500
Monthly Profit shows consistency —
how often you’re profitable month to month.

15
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,500
Now the game-changer:
Optimal SL.

16
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:20,500
It’s a “what-if” simulator:
what if your stops were larger or smaller?

17
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:27,000
Move the slider and TestingView recalculates
the outcome instantly.

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Including TP hits and the full equity curve,
versus your original approach.

19
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,500
You’re not guessing stops —
you’re testing a hypothesis.

20
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:42,500
Same idea for targets:
Optimal TP.

21
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:47,500
Adjust TP size and see the impact instantly:
hit rate and performance.

22
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:53,500
You can see when a bigger TP helps…
and when pushing it too far breaks results.

23
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:58,000
And for realism: trading costs —
spreads and commissions.

24
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,500
Set them as % per lot/contract across all trades,
then copy to clipboard or export to Excel.
